<Slide style={{
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    padding: '0 72px',
    background: '#FFFFFF',
}}>
    <Box style={{ width: '100%', height: 720, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
        <Box style={{
            height: 120,
            paddingTop: 20,
            paddingBottom: 16,
            flexDirection: 'column',
            justifyContent: 'flex-end',
        }}>
            <Box style={{ width: 56, height: 6, background: '#97C459', marginBottom: 14 }} />
            <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#0B1F1A' }}>
                What the system believes, on every event
            </Text>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ height: 540, flexDirection: 'row', gap: 34 }}>
            <Box style={{
                width: 300,
                background: 'linear-gradient(160deg, #04342C 0%, #0F6E56 100%)',
                padding: '28px 24px',
                flexDirection: 'column',
            }}>
                <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 13, color: '#97C459', letterSpacing: 1.6 }}>
                    STATE SNAPSHOTS
                </Text>
                <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.45, marginTop: 18 }}>
                    Every turn event publishes what the system currently believes, precisely enough to act on.
                </Text>
                <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 16, lineHeight: 1.55, color: 'rgba(225,245,238,0.88)', marginTop: 16 }}>
                    An interruption then stops being a special case. It is a comparison of two states, and the difference says
                    exactly what to re-run.
                </Text>
                <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', paddingTop: 18 }}>
                    <Box style={{ height: 1, background: 'rgba(225,245,238,0.28)', marginBottom: 14 }} />
                    <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 13, color: '#97C459' }}>
                        SnapshotJournal
                    </Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 15, lineHeight: 1.5, color: 'rgba(225,245,238,0.82)', marginTop: 6 }}>
                        holds every event in order, so a turn can be replayed rather than guessed at.
                    </Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>

            <Box style={{ width: 802, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 24 }}>
                <Box style={{
                    height: 250,
                    background: '#E1F5EE',
                    padding: '18px 24px',
                    flexDirection: 'column',
                    justifyContent: 'space-between',
                }}>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 12, color: '#0F6E56', letterSpacing: 1.5, width: 200 }}>
                            FIELD
                        </Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 12, color: '#0F6E56', letterSpacing: 1.5, flex: 1 }}>
                            VALUE AFTER “CHANGE THE CITY TO BANGALORE”
                        </Text>
                    </Box>

                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>intent</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0B1F1A', flex: 1 }}>"python backend engineer"</Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>slots.city</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0B1F1A', flex: 1 }}>"bangalore"</Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>slots.must_skills</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0B1F1A', flex: 1 }}>["python"]</Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>slots.min_years_exp</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0B1F1A', flex: 1 }}>5</Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>changed_fields</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#97C459', fontWeight: 'bold', flex: 1 }}>["city"]</Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row' }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56', width: 200 }}>unset_slots</Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 13, color: '#6B7280', flex: 1 }}>
                            7 named: country · max_years_exp · should_skills · should_themes · should_roles · should_locations · excluded_skills
                        </Text>
                    </Box>
                </Box>

                <Box style={{ height: 266, flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24 }}>
                    <Box style={{
                        flex: 1,
                        border: '1px solid #E1F5EE',
                        borderTop: '5px solid #0F6E56',
                        padding: '22px 24px',
                        flexDirection: 'column',
                    }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 21, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#04342C', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                            Slots are total, not sparse
                        </Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 16.5, lineHeight: 1.55, color: '#0B1F1A', marginTop: 12 }}>
                            A snapshot names every constraint slot, including the empty ones. A clarification decision has to tell
                            “the user never mentioned a country” apart from “we dropped the country they gave us” — and an absent
                            field cannot express that difference.
                        </Text>
                    </Box>
                    <Box style={{
                        flex: 1,
                        border: '1px solid #E1F5EE',
                        borderTop: '5px solid #0F6E56',
                        padding: '22px 24px',
                        flexDirection: 'column',
                    }}>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 21, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#04342C', lineHeight: 1.35 }}>
                            The panel shows the diff, not the state
                        </Text>
                        <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 16.5, lineHeight: 1.55, color: '#0B1F1A', marginTop: 12 }}>
                            Every event carries a snapshot, so rendering all of them would bury the conversation. The panel draws
                            one only when <span style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 15, color: '#0F6E56' }}>changed_fields</span> is
                            non-empty or the phase is final — which is why an interruption reads as a visible event rather than noise.
                        </Text>
                    </Box>
                </Box>
            </Box>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{
            height: 60,
            paddingBottom: 20,
            flexDirection: 'row',
            alignItems: 'center',
            justifyContent: 'space-between',
        }}>
            <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 14, color: '#6B7280' }}>
                Talent Atlas · Samsung PRISM Y2026 · Theme 05
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontFamily: 'JetBrains Mono', fontSize: 14, color: '#6B7280' }}>
                07 / 12
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>
</Slide>
